module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.Charts.Descent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.Flat
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj.RelativeDimension
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GradedAlgebraBridge
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.TerminalRelativeProj

/-!
# Section rings of a graded algebra generated in degree one

Let `s` be a relative `Proj` situation: a scheme `s.base` carrying a quasi-coherent,
commutative, nonnegatively graded algebra over its structure sheaf. The geometry of the relative
projective spectrum of `s` — that its structure morphism is locally of finite type, proper, flat,
or of a given relative dimension — is reduced by
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProj/LocalAtBase.lean`,
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProj/Flat.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProj/RelativeDimension.lean` to two facts about the graded
ring of sections over each affine open `U` of the base: that `Γ(S, U)` is carried
isomorphically onto the degree-zero part, and that the section ring is generated over its
degree-zero part by homogeneous elements of positive degree.

This file supplies both from hypotheses on the *sheaf* of graded algebras, so that a consumer
never has to compute with the section rings directly.

The first is `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.isIso_sectionRingZeroMap`: the degree-zero
identification of the charts is an isomorphism as soon as multiplying the algebra unit by a
function on the base is a bijection onto the degree-zero local sections, which is what the
degree-zero piece being the structure sheaf amounts to.

The second starts from `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne`, the assertion that
each positive homogeneous piece is additively generated by products of a degree-one section with
a section of the preceding degree. That assertion is about the sheaf of graded algebras; the
section ring is a direct sum over the *nonnegative* degrees, so passing from one to the other is
an induction that has to move the degree shift `1 + n` of the multiplication onto the index
`n + 1` of the summand, and that is the content of
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne`.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne`: every positive homogeneous piece over an
  object of the site is additively generated by the products of a degree-one section with a
  section of the preceding degree.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.app_natCast_eq_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne` and
  `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.Hom.ext_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne`: **an algebra generated in
  degree one rigidifies its homomorphisms** — two of them agreeing in degrees zero and one agree
  in every nonnegative degree, and agree outright once they also agree in the negative degrees.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.isIso_sectionRingZeroMap`: the degree-zero identification of the
  chart over `U` is an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.bijective_smul_one_of_isoUnit`: its hypothesis holds whenever the
  degree-zero piece of the algebra is identified with the structure sheaf compatibly with the
  units.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne`:
  **the section ring over `U` is generated by its degree-one part over its degree-zero part**,
  as soon as the algebra is generated in degree one over `U`.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.adjoin_range_of_one_eq_top`: the same with the generators given
  as the image of the degree-one local sections, which is the indexed-family form that
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data.flat_toBase_of_flat_away` consumes.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.finiteType_sectionRing`: the section ring is a finite-type
  algebra over its degree-zero part as soon as, in addition, the degree-one local sections are
  spanned by finitely many of them.
* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.locallyOfFiniteType_relativeProjToBase`,
  `isProper_relativeProjToBase`, `isSeparated_relativeProjToBase`,
  `universallyClosed_relativeProjToBase` and `flat_relativeProjToBase`: the geometry of the
  relative projective spectrum of a situation, transferred from the charts of
  `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data` to `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.relativeProjToBase` and stated in
  the situation's own vocabulary.

## Implementation notes

The degree shift is handled by a private additive equivalence `pieceCastAux` transporting a
homogeneous piece along an equality of degrees, rather than by a `rewrite` in the goal: the type
`(A.piece i).val.obj U` is a sheaf-of-modules section group, so a motive mentioning it does not
typecheck at `instance` transparency, and `DirectSum.of_eq_of_gradedMonoid_eq` is the clean way to
compare the two summands afterwards.

Relative dimension needs no counterpart here: `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.relativeProjToBase`
is `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data.toBase` of `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.chartData` by definition,
so `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data.relativeDimension_toBase` applies to it directly, and unlike the
five properties above it is not a `CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty`, so there is nothing to
transfer across the chart isomorphism.

**What the rigidity lemmas do and do not assume.**
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.apply_eq_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne` is the content: it needs
generation in degree one over the *one* object of the site whose sections it compares, which is
what a graded algebra presented by charts actually satisfies — `IsGeneratedInDegreeOne` of a
conormal algebra holds over an affine closed-immersion chart and not over an arbitrary open,
since a homogeneous section of degree `n` over a general open is only *locally* a sum of products.
`app_natCast_eq_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne` and `Hom.ext_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne` quantify over
every object of the site and are therefore the convenient rather than the applicable form: to use
them for an algebra generated in degree one only over a basis one must first descend the
sectionwise agreement from the basis to every open, which is the separatedness of the target
sheaf and is not proved here.

`IsGeneratedInDegreeOne` is stated as a statement about *additive subgroups* — every additive
subgroup of the degree-`1 + n` piece containing all those products is everything — rather than as
an equation between subgroups, because that is the form in which it is used and because the
degree-`1 + n` piece is not a subobject of anything, so there is no ambient object in which to
write the span.

Everything in the `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation` namespace below is about a situation in general
and not about a projective bundle. It lives here rather than in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProj/`, where it belongs, because that directory is being
edited elsewhere; it should be moved there when the two are next touched together.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. Nothing here is one of the assertions of a Stacks tag:
these are the two inputs that tag 02TX's assertions about a projective bundle are reduced to,
not the assertions.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02TX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02TX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01OB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01OB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite DirectSum
open HomogeneousLocalization

universe t a v u

namespace SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{t}}

/-- **The algebra is generated in degree one over an object of the site.** Every additive subgroup
of the degree-`1 + n` local sections which contains every product of a degree-one local section
with a degree-`n` one is the whole group.

For the symmetric algebra of a sheaf of modules this is the sheaf-level form of the statement that
`Symⁿ⁺¹` is spanned by the products of a generator with `Symⁿ`. -/
def IsGeneratedInDegreeOne (A : GradedAlgebra.{t, a} R) (W : Cᵒᵖ) : Prop :=
  ∀ (n : ℕ) (P : AddSubgroup ((A.piece (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.obj W)),
    (∀ (x : (A.piece 1).val.obj W) (y : (A.piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj W),
      (A.mul 1 n).app W x y ∈ P) → P = ⊤

/-! ### Rigidity of homomorphisms out of an algebra generated in degree one -/

section GeneratedInDegreeOne

variable {A B : GradedAlgebra.{t, a} R} {W : Cᵒᵖ}

/-- **Degreewise rigidity.** If `A` is generated in degree one over `W`, two homomorphisms out of
`A` which agree in degree `n` and in degree one agree in degree `1 + n`, on the local sections
over `W`. -/
theorem apply_eq_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne (hA : IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A W) (f g : Hom A B)
    (n : ℕ) (hn : f.app (n : ℤ) = g.app (n : ℤ)) (h1 : f.app 1 = g.app 1)
    (x : (A.piece (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.obj W) :
    (f.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W x = (g.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W x := by
  let P : AddSubgroup ((A.piece (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.obj W) :=
    { carrier := {z | (f.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W z = (g.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W z}
      zero_mem' := by simp
      add_mem' := by
        intro z w hz hw
        change (f.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W (z + w) = _
        change (f.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W z = _ at hz
        change (f.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W w = _ at hw
        rw [map_add, map_add, hz, hw]
      neg_mem' := by
        intro z hz
        change (f.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W (-z) = _
        change (f.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W z = _ at hz
        rw [map_neg, map_neg, hz] }
  have hprod : ∀ (y : (A.piece 1).val.obj W) (z : (A.piece (n : ℤ)).val.obj W),
      (A.mul 1 n).app W y z ∈ P := by
    intro y z
    change (f.app (1 + (n : ℤ))).val.app W ((A.mul 1 n).app W y z) = _
    rw [f.map_mul 1 (n : ℤ) W y z, h1, hn, ← g.map_mul 1 (n : ℤ) W y z]
  have htop : P = ⊤ := hA n P hprod
  have hmem : x ∈ P := htop ▸ AddSubgroup.mem_top x
  exact hmem

/-- **Two homomorphisms out of an algebra generated in degree one over every object of the site
which agree in degrees zero and one agree in every nonnegative degree.** This is the uniqueness
input for extending an identification of the degree-zero and degree-one pieces of a graded
algebra generated in degree one. -/
theorem app_natCast_eq_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne
    (hA : ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ, IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A W) (f g : Hom A B)
    (h0 : f.app 0 = g.app 0) (h1 : f.app 1 = g.app 1) (n : ℕ) :
    f.app (n : ℤ) = g.app (n : ℤ) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simpa using h0
  | succ n hn =>
      have hcast : ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) = 1 + (n : ℤ) := by push_cast; ring
      rw [hcast]
      apply SheafOfModules.hom_ext
      apply PresheafOfModules.Hom.ext
      funext V
      ext x
      exact apply_eq_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne (hA V) f g n hn h1 x

/-- **Homomorphisms out of an algebra generated in degree one are determined by their degree-zero
and degree-one components**, once they are known to agree in the negative degrees. When the
negative pieces of `A` vanish the last hypothesis is supplied by
`CategoryTheory.Limits.IsZero.eq_of_src`. -/
theorem Hom.ext_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne
    (hA : ∀ W : Cᵒᵖ, IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A W) {f g : Hom A B}
    (hneg : ∀ n : ℤ, n < 0 → f.app n = g.app n)
    (h0 : f.app 0 = g.app 0) (h1 : f.app 1 = g.app 1) : f = g := by
  refine Hom.ext fun n => ?_
  rcases lt_or_ge n 0 with hlt | hge
  · exact hneg n hlt
  · obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := Int.eq_ofNat_of_zero_le hge
    exact app_natCast_eq_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne hA f g h0 h1 m

end GeneratedInDegreeOne

end SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra

namespace Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation

variable (s : Situation.{u})

/-! ### The degree-zero identification -/

/-- Multiplying the algebra unit by a function on the base is a bijection onto the degree-zero
local sections, whenever the degree-zero piece of the algebra is identified with the structure
sheaf by an isomorphism carrying the unit to `1`. The inverse is that isomorphism. -/
theorem bijective_smul_one_of_isoUnit
    (e : s.algebra.piece 0 ≅ SheafOfModules.unit s.base.ringCatSheaf)
    (he : ∀ W : (TopologicalSpace.Opens s.base)ᵒᵖ,
      e.hom.val.app W (s.algebra.one.eval W) = (1 : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj W))
    (U : s.base.Opens) :
    Function.Bijective
      (fun r : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U) => r • s.algebra.one.eval (op U)) := by
  refine ⟨fun r r' hr => ?_, fun x =>
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.exists_smul_one_of_isoUnit s.algebra e he (op U) x⟩
  have key (t : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) :
      e.hom.val.app (op U) (t • s.algebra.one.eval (op U)) = t := by
    rw [map_smul, he]
    exact mul_one t
  rw [← key r, ← key r']
  exact congrArg (e.hom.val.app (op U)) hr

/-- **The degree-zero identification of the chart over `U` is an isomorphism**, as soon as
multiplying the algebra unit by a function on the base is a bijection onto the degree-zero local
sections over `U`.

This is the hypothesis `hb` of every transfer result of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProj/LocalAtBase.lean`. -/
theorem isIso_sectionRingZeroMap (U : s.base.Opens)
    (hbij : Function.Bijective
      (fun r : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U) => r • s.algebra.one.eval (op U))) :
    IsIso (sectionRingZeroMap s U) := by
  have key (r : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) :
      GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (s.sectionRingGrading U) (s.sectionRingBaseMap U r) =
        ⟨s.sectionRingBaseMap U r, sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero s U r⟩ :=
    GradedRing.projZeroRingHom'_apply_coe _ ⟨_, sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero s U r⟩
  have hval (r : s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U)) :
      s.sectionRingBaseMap U r =
        DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 0 (r • s.algebra.one.eval (op U)) :=
    (sectionRingStructure s).baseMap_apply U r
  rw [ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective]
  refine ⟨fun r r' hr => ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hr' : GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (s.sectionRingGrading U)
        (s.sectionRingBaseMap U r) =
          GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (s.sectionRingGrading U)
            (s.sectionRingBaseMap U r') := hr
    have h0 : s.sectionRingBaseMap U r = s.sectionRingBaseMap U r' :=
      congrArg Subtype.val ((key r).symm.trans (hr'.trans (key r')))
    exact hbij.injective (DirectSum.of_injective (β := s.sectionPieces U) 0
      ((hval r).symm.trans (h0.trans (hval r'))))
  · rintro ⟨y, b, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hbij.surjective b
    refine ⟨r, ?_⟩
    change GradedRing.projZeroRingHom' (s.sectionRingGrading U) (s.sectionRingBaseMap U r) = _
    rw [key r]
    exact Subtype.ext ((hval r).trans (congrArg (DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 0) hr))

/-! ### Generation in degree one -/

/-- Transport of a homogeneous local section along an equality of degrees. Stated as an additive
equivalence rather than as a `rewrite` in the goal, since a motive mentioning a section group of
a sheaf of modules does not typecheck at `instance` transparency. -/
private def pieceCastAux (U : s.base.Opens) {i j : ℤ} (h : i = j) :
    (s.algebra.piece i).val.obj (op U) ≃+ (s.algebra.piece j).val.obj (op U) := by
  subst h; exact AddEquiv.refl _

private theorem pieceCastAux_heq (U : s.base.Opens) {i j : ℤ} (h : i = j)
    (x : (s.algebra.piece i).val.obj (op U)) : pieceCastAux s U h x ≍ x := by
  subst h; rfl

/-- The product in the section ring of a degree-one and a degree-`n` homogeneous local section is
their product in the graded algebra, placed in the degree-`n + 1` summand. -/
private theorem of_mul_of_degree_one (U : s.base.Opens) (n : ℕ) (x : s.sectionPieces U 1)
    (y : s.sectionPieces U n) :
    DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) (n + 1)
        (pieceCastAux s U (show (1 : ℤ) + (n : ℤ) = ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) by omega)
          ((s.algebra.mul 1 n).app (op U) x y)) =
      DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x * DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n y := by
  rw [DirectSum.of_mul_of]
  refine DirectSum.of_eq_of_gradedMonoid_eq (Sigma.ext (Nat.add_comm n 1) ?_)
  exact (pieceCastAux_heq s U _ _).trans
    ((sectionRingStructure s).mul_homogeneous U 1 n x y).symm

/-- **The section ring over `U` is generated by its degree-one part over its degree-zero part**,
as soon as the graded algebra is generated in degree one over `U`.

The induction is on the degree of a homogeneous summand. In the step from `n` to `n + 1` the
additive subgroup of degree-`1 + n` local sections whose image in the section ring lies in the
subalgebra contains every product of a degree-one section with a degree-`n` one, by the inductive
hypothesis, so generation in degree one makes it everything. -/
theorem adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne (U : s.base.Opens)
    (hgen : s.algebra.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne (op U)) :
    Algebra.adjoin (s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
      (s.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) = ⊤ := by
  set D := Algebra.adjoin (s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
    (s.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) with hD
  have hone (x : s.sectionPieces U 1) : DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x ∈ D :=
    Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨x, rfl⟩
  have hmem (n : ℕ) (x : s.sectionPieces U n) :
      DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) n x ∈ D := by
    induction n with
    | zero => exact D.algebraMap_mem ⟨_, ⟨x, rfl⟩⟩
    | succ n ih =>
        set c := pieceCastAux s U (show (1 : ℤ) + (n : ℤ) = ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) by omega) with hc
        set P := D.toSubring.toAddSubgroup.comap
          ((DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) (n + 1)).comp c.toAddMonoidHom) with hPdef
        have hP : P = ⊤ := hgen n P fun z w => by
          change DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) (n + 1)
            (c ((s.algebra.mul 1 n).app (op U) z w)) ∈ D
          rw [of_mul_of_degree_one]
          exact D.mul_mem (hone z) (ih w)
        obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := c.surjective x
        exact show w ∈ P from hP.symm ▸ AddSubgroup.mem_top w
  refine top_unique fun x _ => ?_
  induction x using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => exact D.zero_mem
  | of n x => exact hmem n x
  | add x y hx hy => exact D.add_mem (hx trivial) (hy trivial)

/-- The degree-one part of the section ring, as the image of the degree-one local sections. This
is the indexed-family form of the generating set. -/
theorem range_of_one (U : s.base.Opens) :
    Set.range (fun x : s.sectionPieces U 1 => DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x) =
      (s.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) := by
  ext z
  exact ⟨fun ⟨x, hx⟩ => ⟨x, hx⟩, fun ⟨x, hx⟩ => ⟨x, hx⟩⟩

/-- **The section ring over `U` is generated by the images of the degree-one local sections.** This
is the form `Stacks.RelativeProj.Data.flat_toBase_of_flat_away` asks for: a family of homogeneous
elements of positive degree generating the section ring over its degree-zero part. -/
theorem adjoin_range_of_one_eq_top (U : s.base.Opens)
    (hgen : s.algebra.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne (op U)) :
    Algebra.adjoin (s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
        (Set.range fun x : s.sectionPieces U 1 => DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x) = ⊤ := by
  rw [range_of_one]
  exact adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne s U hgen

/-- **The section ring over `U` is a finite-type algebra over its degree-zero part**, as soon as
the graded algebra is generated in degree one over `U` and the degree-one local sections over `U`
are spanned by finitely many of them.

This is the hypothesis `hft` of the finite-type, proper and universally-closed transfer results of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProj/LocalAtBase.lean`. For the symmetric algebra of a
module generated by `r` sections the spanning family is the image of those sections in degree
one. -/
theorem finiteType_sectionRing (U : s.base.Opens)
    (hgen : s.algebra.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne (op U)) (g : Finset (s.sectionPieces U 1))
    (hg : Submodule.span (s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))
      (g : Set (s.sectionPieces U 1)) = ⊤) :
    Algebra.FiniteType (s.sectionRingGrading U 0) (s.sectionRing U) := by
  classical
  set S := Algebra.adjoin (s.sectionRingGrading U 0)
    ((fun x : s.sectionPieces U 1 => DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x) ''
      (g : Set (s.sectionPieces U 1))) with hS
  have key : (s.sectionRingGrading U 1 : Set (s.sectionRing U)) ⊆ S := by
    rintro z ⟨x, rfl⟩
    have hx : x ∈ Submodule.span (s.base.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op U))
        (g : Set (s.sectionPieces U 1)) := hg ▸ trivial
    induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem y hy => exact Algebra.subset_adjoin ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact S.zero_mem
    | add y w _ _ ihy ihw => rw [map_add]; exact S.add_mem ihy ihw
    | smul r y _ ih =>
        rw [← sectionRingBaseMap_mul_of s U 1 r y]
        exact S.mul_mem (S.algebraMap_mem
          (⟨s.sectionRingBaseMap U r, sectionRingBaseMap_mem_zero s U r⟩ :
            s.sectionRingGrading U 0)) ih
  refine ⟨⟨g.image fun x => DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U) 1 x, ?_⟩⟩
  rw [Finset.coe_image]
  refine top_unique ?_
  rw [← adjoin_sectionRingGrading_one_eq_top_of_isGeneratedInDegreeOne s U hgen]
  exact Algebra.adjoin_le key

/-! ### The geometry of the relative projective spectrum of a situation -/

/-- **The structure morphism of the relative projective spectrum of a situation is locally of
finite type** when every section ring is a finite-type algebra over its degree-zero part. -/
theorem locallyOfFiniteType_relativeProjToBase
    (hb : ∀ U : s.base.affineOpens, IsIso (sectionRingZeroMap s U.1))
    (hft : ∀ U : s.base.affineOpens,
      Algebra.FiniteType (s.sectionRingGrading U.1 0) (s.sectionRing U.1)) :
    LocallyOfFiniteType (relativeProjToBase s) :=
  (chartData s).locallyOfFiniteType_toBase hb hft

/-- **The structure morphism of the relative projective spectrum of a situation is proper** when
every section ring is a finite-type algebra over its degree-zero part. -/
theorem isProper_relativeProjToBase
    (hb : ∀ U : s.base.affineOpens, IsIso (sectionRingZeroMap s U.1))
    (hft : ∀ U : s.base.affineOpens,
      Algebra.FiniteType (s.sectionRingGrading U.1 0) (s.sectionRing U.1)) :
    IsProper (relativeProjToBase s) :=
  (chartData s).isProper_toBase hb hft

/-- **The structure morphism of the relative projective spectrum of a situation is universally
closed** when every section ring is a finite-type algebra over its degree-zero part. -/
theorem universallyClosed_relativeProjToBase
    (hb : ∀ U : s.base.affineOpens, IsIso (sectionRingZeroMap s U.1))
    (hft : ∀ U : s.base.affineOpens,
      Algebra.FiniteType (s.sectionRingGrading U.1 0) (s.sectionRing U.1)) :
    UniversallyClosed (relativeProjToBase s) :=
  (chartData s).universallyClosed_toBase hb hft

/-- **The structure morphism of the relative projective spectrum of a situation is flat** when
the graded algebra is generated in degree one over every affine open of the base and every
degree-zero homogeneous localization at a degree-one local section is flat.

Generation in degree one is what makes the images of the degree-one local sections a generating
family of homogeneous elements of positive degree, which is what the chartwise flatness criterion
of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProj/Flat.lean` consumes. -/
theorem flat_relativeProjToBase
    (hb : ∀ U : s.base.affineOpens, IsIso (sectionRingZeroMap s U.1))
    (hgen : ∀ U : s.base.affineOpens, s.algebra.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne (op U.1))
    (hflat : ∀ (U : s.base.affineOpens) (x : s.sectionPieces U.1 1),
      Module.Flat (s.sectionRingGrading U.1 0)
        (Away (s.sectionRingGrading U.1) (DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U.1) 1 x))) :
    Flat (relativeProjToBase s) := by
  have hg : ∀ (U : s.base.affineOpens) (x : s.sectionPieces U.1 1),
      DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U.1) 1 x ∈ s.sectionRingGrading U.1 1 :=
    fun _ x => AddMonoidHom.mem_range.mpr ⟨x, rfl⟩
  exact (chartData s).flat_toBase_of_flat_away hb
    (fun U x => DirectSum.of (s.sectionPieces U.1) 1 x) (fun _ _ => 1) (fun _ _ => Nat.one_pos)
    hg (fun U => adjoin_range_of_one_eq_top s U.1 (hgen U)) hflat

end Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation

